        "id": 19070,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-29T04:01:34.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I'm struggling through a Source of All Foes game with never enough Aeon Men or enough damage, and saw an opportunity to make an unconventional play that might save me. (Or more accurately, make me maybe slightly less screwed.) Unfortunately, Dark Conductor Argent Adept can't seem to flip an Aeon Man into play with his power. It is automatically discarded each time. The hero or environment cards are played automatically. Picking the Aeon Man deck and the Scion deck causes the Aeon Man to be discarded, and the Scion card to just kinda vanish without effect.</p>\n<p>Aeon Master (Grim Sacrificer) is in the play area, with a few Thralls. OblivAeon is not. There are no cards that block plays out. I just wanted to double-check that I'm not missing an obscure line in the rules or a known issue before making a bug report.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:52:37.506Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 5,
