      {
        "id": 226193,
        "name": "FearLord",
        "username": "FearLord",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/5f8ce5/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2019-03-29T09:37:50.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>There’s a line in the rules that states that cards from the Aeon Men deck don’t have a play phase and that they are only played when instructed by ObliVeon or a Scion card, but I think that’s more to clarify that you only play them when told to... the clarification section clarifies that it is a Villain deck, and it’s very specific that you can only target the deck if there is a card from that deck in that battle zone (and that the mission deck can’t be targeted by effects) so I don’t see any reason this shouldn’t work - I’d report it as a bug.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:00:02.376Z",
